{
  "id": "COMPOUND:35963 - PROTEIN:5826",
  "verbalization": "Picrasin F is implicated in the biological activity against SMMC-7721 through multiple pathways, all of which converge on the enzyme CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase. This enzyme is a target of several compounds, including 2,4-Bis[(4-hydroxyphenyl)methyl]-5-methoxy-3-[2-(3-methoxyphenyl)ethyl]phenol and (1S,3E,4S,5S,6S)-4,5-dihydroxy-3-(3-methylbut-2-enylidene)-7-oxabicyclo[4.1.0]heptan-2-one, which both direct their targets to SMMC-7721. Picrasin F's relationship with SMMC-7721 is thus mediated through this enzyme, suggesting a potential role in modulating cellular processes in the cancer cell line. The evidence supports a mechanism where Picrasin F may influence SMMC-7721 through the regulation of this enzyme, though the exact functional pathway remains to be fully elucidated.",
